<article class="env-lemma" id="0G0J">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G0J">Lemma <span data-tag="0G0J">57.15.2</span>.</a> With notation as in Definition <a href="/tag/0G0I" data-tag="0G0I">57.15.1</a> let $K$ be the Fourier-Mukai kernel of a relative equivalence from $X$ to $Y$ over $S$. Then the corresponding Fourier-Mukai functors $\Phi _ K : D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X) \to D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ Y)$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/0FYR" data-tag="0FYR">57.8.2</a>) and $\Phi _ K : D_{perf}(\mathcal{O}_ X) \to D_{perf}(\mathcal{O}_ Y)$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/0FYT" data-tag="0FYT">57.8.4</a>) are equivalences. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate from Lemma <a href="/tag/0FYS" data-tag="0FYS">57.8.3</a> and Example <a href="/tag/0FYV" data-tag="0FYV">57.8.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>